- `branch(b1, XOR)` (with `precedence(n3, b1)` and `precedence(b1, n4)`): The source describes a strictly linear progression (“check if the user has already liked the company and save the action”) with no conditional routing or alternative paths. Inserting an XOR gateway with only a single successor hallucinates a decision structure and misrepresents the intended control flow (violates SMC1, SMC4).
- `defines(v1, "Has the user already liked the company", {})`: The source does not introduce a decision variable or specify its value domain. Declaring it with an empty range `{}` fails to capture the implied binary/contextual nature of the verification step, and the variable is never used in any guard condition (violates SMC1, SMC6).

Structural Check
- [S1] STC9 failed: Each branch node must have exactly one incoming and at least two outgoing edges. | Node `b1` has in=1 and out=1. | DSL: branch(b1,XOR)
- [S2] STC11 failed: Each variable definition must have a valid range with at least two distinct values. | Variable `v1` has an invalid range `[]`.
- [S3] STC16 failed: Every outgoing edge of XOR/OR branches must have exactly one guard. | XOR/OR edge `b1 -> n4` has 0 guards; exactly one is required.